module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Homology.ShortComplex.ModuleCat
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.ConcreteCategory.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.Modules.GlobalSectionLinear
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Algebra.AdicLimitTopology
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.InverseSystems.TorsionFreeAndDivisibleSystems

/-!
# The `f`-adic topology on the limit of the cohomology of an inverse system

Let `O` be a sheaf of commutative rings on a site, let `f` be a global section of `O` and let
`… → 𝓕₂ → 𝓕₁` be an inverse system of `O`-modules satisfying condition (1) of Stacks 0H39 for
multiplication by `f`: multiplication by `f` on `𝓕ₙ₊₁` factors through the transition map
`𝓕ₙ₊₁ → 𝓕ₙ` and `0 → 𝓕ₙ → 𝓕ₙ₊₁ → 𝓕₁ → 0` is short exact. Write `Hᵖ = lim Hᵖ(C, 𝓕ₙ)`. Then

`f^c · Hᵖ = ker (Hᵖ → Hᵖ(C, 𝓕_c))` for every `c ≥ 1`,

and consequently the inverse-limit topology on `Hᵖ` is the `f`-adic topology.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.InverseSystems.range_pow_eq_ker_limitProjection`: the `f^c`-multiples in
  `lim Hᵖ(C, 𝓕ₙ)` are exactly the compatible classes vanishing in `Hᵖ(C, 𝓕_c)`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.InverseSystems.limitCohomologyTopology_eq_adic`: consequently the
  inverse-limit topology on `lim Hᵖ(C, 𝓕ₙ)` is the topology defined by the principal ideal
  generated by `f`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.InverseSystems.range_pow_eq_ker_limitProjection_and_limitTopology_eq_adic`:
  both statements together.

## Implementation notes

As in `Stacks.Cohomology.InverseSystems.TorsionFreeDivisible`, the system is indexed from zero,
`obj n` standing for `𝓕ₙ₊₁`; the kernel formula for `𝓕_c` with `c = n + 1 ≥ 1` is therefore stated
at the index `n` with exponent `n + 1`.

Condition (1) of Stacks 0H39 is stated for modules in the universe `max u v`, so the structure
sheaf is taken in that universe as well.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H39](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H39)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open scoped IsMulCommutative

universe u v w a m

namespace Stacks.Cohomology.InverseSystems

open Stacks.Cohomology.InverseSystems.TorsionFreeDivisible (Condition1 mulF_naturality proj)
open Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules (GlobalSectionRing cohomologyDeltaFunctor
